{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage","id":1554935,"title":"Artificer Build for Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-01T20:13:51-07:00","id":1554935,"title":"Artificer Build for Mage","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I have an idea for a somewhat unconventional Mage character. They\u2019d be closer to an Artificer (from D&amp;D 3.5) than a typical Awakened Mage. Alternately, they could be a pseudo-Technomancer of sorts, depending on whether I go with a \u201cMagick Items\u201d or \u201cHypertech Devices\u201d approach. The latter would probably attract less Paradox.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The general gist is to combine the Sanctum Background with the Phylactery Flaw. In this case the Phylactery is either the location itself or something like an altar or statue whose presence makes the area around it into a Sanctum; it\u2019s big and awkward to move, so you can\u2019t run around town with it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Benefit: I never have to deal with Paradox. Outside of my Sanctum, Paradox can affect my <b><i>items</i></b>, but not <b><i>me</i></b>.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Drawback: Loss of flexibility. I can\u2019t just whip out spells whenever and however I please.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">One idea I\u2019d also like to pursue is from M20 The Book of Secret, p. 161:</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u201cTechnocratic Union facilities produce Devices and Principiae without the Willpower or personal Quintessence requirements. Individual technomancers and Technocrats, however, must invest Willpower and personal Quintessence into their Devices.\u201d</span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Now, as far I\u2019m concerned, you don\u2019t get to just throw that out there and not include rules for it. The idea seems to be that you substitute enough Quintessence to make up for not sacrificing Willpower points. The questions are then how many and how do you set up your personal facilities to be able to do this? So, I\u2019d be looking to get my workshop up and going with that ability as well. Invest some points in the Node Background and I should have a pretty good magical items production facility.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Thoughts or suggestions?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28819,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","user":"Arcanum Scholar","date":". 11-02-2025, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T22:28:15-07:00","id":1554939,"title":"","content":"About TU facilities, AFAIK, &quot;just throwing that out there and not include rules for it&quot; it's exactly what they did. You would need a house rule for that.<br /> <br /> The only thing that's explicitly ruled in BoS it's that the facility allows to ignore those requisites, and that this is a property of the facility itself, not the mage (an &quot;individual&quot; Technocrat, in spite of having the correct Focus and affiliation, can't benefit from this advantage).<br /> <br /> I joke that, as far as we know, TU could be kidnapping orphan children to drain their willpower for use in their Devices - not that I think this is what happens, but the point it's that there's no proof, AFAIK, that it does not happen. MECHA worked a bit like that, after all :P<br /> <br /> It could be something akin to Do, something intrinsec to their Focus that requires a special preparation. Or it could be a special &quot;procedure&quot; to create a Device-Factory (probably involving high level spheres) that only the Technocracy knows about, a bit like how Hermetics have their Parma Magica, or how only Technocrats, Etherites and Children of Knowledge know how to make Primium<br /> <br /> Not sure where you've read that having &quot;enough Quintessence&quot; can replace Willpower, but I think such a glaring exception should require an explicit ruling, because a mage can have, individually, lots of Quintessence. If it was something you can have with just a Node, something you can get at char-gen, I think that an explicit ruling it's a <i>must</i>.<br /> <br /> But ST can rule that this is the case, after all, AFAIK, it's not ruled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-02-2025, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T22:50:25-07:00","id":1554940,"title":"","content":"First of all, I don't think this is unconventional. It's basically most <b>Prime</b> Mages with a <b>Sanctum</b>.<br /> <br /> And indeed you get the benefit with <b>Sanctum</b> alone, all that <b>Phylactery</b> does here is to prevent you from even trying Magic on the run. And even then, <b>Phylactery</b> was specifically worded with this option in mind.<br /> <br /> Wonder creation requires <i><b>both </b></i>willpower and Quintessence, so I think you misread something here. There's nothing about using Quint to bypass the Will cost.<br /> <br /> The rules for Technocratic facilities ignoring costs aren't given because they're not meant to be replicated. Setting-as-intended, any Mage who finds out how to replicate the single greatest asset of the Union has in their hands a world-changing secret of epic proportions.<br /> <br /> It is, for all intents and purposes, for them and them only. Unless, of course, the ST deliberately chooses to run things differently.<br /> <br /> So there's no rule for it. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> said it's a property of their laboratories and factories, not their Agents, but other than that you'll have to homebrew with no starting point.<br /> <br /> By the way: if anyone knows how the Technocracy gets to run things like that, it's someone extremely high in their hierarchy. Depending on how the current setting is in your chronicle, there may not even be anyone alive that knows how to do it, and the Union be left with whatever production lines survived the Avatar Storm or were retaken since. It may or may not require direct work from an Archmage to make it, or at least someone with Arete/Enlightenment 8+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T22:57:53-07:00","id":1554941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554939#post1554939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About TU facilities, AFAIK, &quot;just throwing that out there and not include rules for it&quot; it's exactly what they did. You would need a house rule for that.<br /> <br /> The only thing that's explicitly ruled in BoS it's that the facility allows to ignore those requisites, and that this is a property of the facility itself, not the mage (an &quot;individual&quot; Technocrat, in spite of having the correct Focus and affiliation, can't benefit from this advantage).<br /> <br /> I joke that, as far as we know, TU could be kidnapping orphan children to drain their willpower for use in their Devices - not that I think this is what happens, but the point it's that there's no proof, AFAIK, that it does not happen. MECHA worked a bit like that, after all :P<br /> <br /> It could be something akin to Do, something intrinsec to their Focus that requires a special preparation. Or it could be a special &quot;procedure&quot; to create a Device-Factory (probably involving high level spheres) that only the Technocracy knows about, a bit like how Hermetics have their Parma Magica, or how only Technocrats, Etherites and Children of Knowledge know how to make Primium<br /> <br /> Not sure where you've read that having &quot;enough Quintessence&quot; can replace Willpower, but I think such a glaring exception should require an explicit ruling, because a mage can have, individually, lots of Quintessence. If it was something you can have with just a Node, something you can get at char-gen, I think that an explicit ruling it's a <i>must</i>.<br /> <br /> But ST can rule that this is the case, after all, AFAIK, it's not ruled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm well aware they didn't include rules for this. That was my point - they <i><b>should</b></i> have. If it's possible in-game, then tell us how it's done. But, they haven't so I'm clearly going to have to house-rule this situation, the only question is how. My best guess as to how they're doing it in canon is by throwing enough points of Quintessence at the problem to make up for the missing Willpower. In which case, what's the conversion rate? 5 points of Quintessence spent = 1 point of Willpower? 10 points of Quintessence?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T23:14:20-07:00","id":1554942,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554940#post1554940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, I don't think this is unconventional. It's basically most <b>Prime</b> Mages with a <b>Sanctum</b>.<br /> <br /> And indeed you get the benefit with <b>Sanctum</b> alone, all that <b>Phylactery</b> does here is to prevent you from even trying Magic on the run. And even then, <b>Phylactery</b> was specifically worded with this option in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Yes, the rules do appear to support this option, but I\u2019ve never actually run across another player who\u2019s done this in Mage. I\u2019m guessing the gamers I hang around with are more conventional in their choice of characters, but maybe you\u2019ve seen this type of character plenty of times already. I haven\u2019t.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554940#post1554940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder creation requires <i><b>both </b></i>willpower and Quintessence, so I think you misread something here. There's nothing about using Quint to bypass the Will cost.<br /> <br /> The rules for Technocratic facilities ignoring costs aren't given because they're not meant to be replicated. Setting-as-intended, any Mage who finds out how to replicate the single greatest asset of the Union has in their hands a world-changing secret of epic proportions.<br /> <br /> It is, for all intents and purposes, for them and them only. Unless, of course, the ST deliberately chooses to run things differently.<br /> <br /> So there's no rule for it. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> said it's a property of their laboratories and factories, not their Agents, but other than that you'll have to homebrew with no starting point.<br /> <br /> By the way: if anyone knows how the Technocracy gets to run things like that, it's someone extremely high in their hierarchy. Depending on how the current setting is in your chronicle, there may not even be anyone alive that knows how to do it, and the Union be left with whatever production lines survived the Avatar Storm or were retaken since. It may or may not require direct work from an Archmage to make it, or at least someone with Arete/Enlightenment 8+.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I\u2019m well aware of the canon rules for magic item creation. I\u2019m also well aware that in canon the Technocracy gets to go \u201cNya, nya, nya, nya, nya \u2013 we\u2019re not restricted those rules! Ha-ha! Sucks to be you!\u201d And I call bullshit. What\u2019s good for the goose is good for the gander. NPCs don\u2019t get the super-cool exotic stuff while the PCs are stuck with the boring stuff. That\u2019s a personal rule of mine that I believe very strongly in. Any time I run across that situation in canon in <i><b>any</b></i> RPG, I immediately rectify it. No special privileges for NPCs. One set of rules for <i><b>everyone</b></i>.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-01T23:58:14-07:00","id":1554944,"title":"","content":"The rules that are needed are: how does one set up a TU construction facility? The rules for <i>using </i>one are already there: enter the facility, go through the usual Wonder-crafting process, and skip the steps involving Personal Quintessence in order to make rolls and expending Willpower in order to finish it. (Note that it <i>doesn't </i>remove the usual requirement to incorporate Quintessence into the Device being made; only the &quot;surcharge&quot; that's needed to make the rolls.) What's involved in setting it up? That's a proprietary TU secret; which, to me, means that it's something that you need the Primal Utility Sphere variant to do; probably at 5 dots, or more. It's not something that player characters can do; not even Technocratic protagonists. <br /> <br /> One possibility would be to say that setting up the facility works a bit like the Terranorming system found in the Operative's Dossier, and/or involves incorporating a Node into the process. Given the TU, that Node stands a good chance of being a Primal Venture. Basically, you have to rewrite the local Reality Zone to permit mass production of Wonders. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T00:26:05-07:00","id":1554946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554944#post1554944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules that are needed are: how does one set up a TU construction facility? The rules for <i>using </i>one are already there: enter the facility, go through the usual Wonder-crafting process, and skip the steps involving Personal Quintessence in order to make rolls and expending Willpower in order to finish it. (Note that it <i>doesn't </i>remove the usual requirement to incorporate Quintessence into the Device being made; only the &quot;surcharge&quot; that's needed to make the rolls.) What's involved in setting it up? That's a proprietary TU secret; which, to me, means that it's something that you need the Primal Utility Sphere variant to do; probably at 5 dots, or more. It's not something that player characters can do; not even Technocratic protagonists.<br /> <br /> One possibility would be to say that setting up the facility works a bit like the Terranorming system found in the Operative's Dossier, and/or involves incorporating a Node into the process. Given the TU, that Node stands a good chance of being a Primal Venture. Basically, you have to rewrite the local Reality Zone to permit mass production of Wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I don't believe in special privileges for NPCs. No &quot;proprietary secrets&quot; allowed. If they can do it in-game, show me the rules. Or they can't do it, either - pick one. As far as setting up a local Reality Zone with a Node, well, that's exactly I'm looking to do. Turn my Sanctum into a magical item production facility, complete with attached Node. Sanctum 5 and Node 5. That ought to do it. (I should also mention that I always take Prime as my Affinity Sphere as well. Honestly, I'm still confused why more Mage players <i><b>don't</b></i>...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T03:41:27-08:00","id":1554954,"title":"","content":"Because the mechanics around affinity Spheres are largely meaningless (and largely backwards from what the game should incentivize IMO). The biggest thing you get is a reduction in XP costs, but it's a pittance given the expense of Spheres and Arete as they are. The most you can save is 10 XP, and that's only if you leave your affinity Sphere at 1 at start. If you want to start making Wonders as fast as possible, you're better leaving Prime as a normal Sphere and giving your Affinity pick to a Sphere you want your items to use. This is even more true if you want to make Wonders out of Spheres that have really good rank 1 and 2 effects. If you want to make a lot of Mind-based Wonders, Mind 1 has lots of cool powers you can put into things with Prime, and only gets better with time so you can at least get your 10 XP. Life 2 is all you need to make healing items. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 11-02-2025, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T05:21:16-08:00","id":1554955,"title":"","content":"Look at <b>Wonder Spheres</b> they're in the <b>Sons of Ether</b> handbook. Basically, <b>Wonder Spheres </b>cost less than regular spheres but are only available for building Talismans techno or otherwise. <b>Arete</b> is still a limit, but the idea works for a Mage of any tradition to work with devices (Wonders) rather than rotes or spontaneous magics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T14:20:01-08:00","id":1554984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554946#post1554946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I don't believe in special privileges for NPCs. No &quot;proprietary secrets&quot; allowed. If they can do it in-game, show me the rules. Or they can't do it, either - pick one.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to get so defensive; I wasn't attacking you, or your idea. I wasn't saying that it can't be done. In particular, Primal Utility isn't an NPCs-only option. Officially, it's a TU-only option; but I have no problem whatsoever with any mage with an appropriate Focus (probably but not certainly practicing the Art of Desire/Hypereconomics) having it. <br /> <br /> But Primal Utility <i>is</i> different from Prime, both in terms of some of the things it can't do (no manifesting swords made entirely out of Quintessence) and in terms of things it <i>can</i> do (until RBGtM, it held a monopoly on accessing Primal Ventures; and even now, it has the edge on making Wonders, as you only need three dots instead of four for Devices). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554946#post1554946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as setting up a local Reality Zone with a Node, well, that's exactly I'm looking to do. Turn my Sanctum into a magical item production facility, complete with attached Node. Sanctum 5 and Node 5. That ought to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There you go, then. Though if I were the Storyteller, I'd also call for Primal Utility instead of Prime. <br /> <br /> And I would second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a>'s advice concerning Wonder Spheres, if your Storyteller will allow it. Basically, you get a price break because you're saddling yourself with a massive restriction, the inability to do anything with it <i>other than </i>make Wonders. <br /> <br /> Also, don't overlook Charms/Gadgets. They're a lot easier to make than Talismans/Devices and are just as shareable; their only downside is that you use them up and have to make more. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T16:37:42-08:00","id":1554992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554954#post1554954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the mechanics around affinity Spheres are largely meaningless (and largely backwards from what the game should incentivize IMO). The biggest thing you get is a reduction in XP costs, but it's a pittance given the expense of Spheres and Arete as they are. The most you can save is 10 XP, and that's only if you leave your affinity Sphere at 1 at start. If you want to start making Wonders as fast as possible, you're better leaving Prime as a normal Sphere and giving your Affinity pick to a Sphere you want your items to use. This is even more true if you want to make Wonders out of Spheres that have really good rank 1 and 2 effects. If you want to make a lot of Mind-based Wonders, Mind 1 has lots of cool powers you can put into things with Prime, and only gets better with time so you can at least get your 10 XP. Life 2 is all you need to make healing items. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, its role in magic item production is fairly critical, and at mastery level you're rolling in all the Quintessence you could ever ask for and can even nullify Paradox. As the foundational Sphere of magic, I've always prioritized it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T16:39:27-08:00","id":1554993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554955#post1554955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at <b>Wonder Spheres</b> they're in the <b>Sons of Ether</b> handbook. Basically, <b>Wonder Spheres </b>cost less than regular spheres but are only available for building Talismans techno or otherwise. <b>Arete</b> is still a limit, but the idea works for a Mage of any tradition to work with devices (Wonders) rather than rotes or spontaneous magics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely missed those! Yes, those are <i><b>absolutely perfect</b></i> for the character I have in mind. I have the Sons of Ether (Revised) sourcebook and there was that optional rule. Thank you very much. :-)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T17:03:24-08:00","id":1554994,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554984#post1554984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No need to get so defensive; I wasn't attacking you, or your idea. I wasn't saying that it can't be done. In particular, Primal Utility isn't an NPCs-only option. Officially, it's a TU-only option; but I have no problem whatsoever with any mage with an appropriate Focus (probably but not certainly practicing the Art of Desire/Hypereconomics) having it.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Sorry, that\u2019s just a long-standing pet peeve of mine, going back decades at this point. I\u2019ve seen plenty of games where the developers go \u201cLook at these super cool things! And you don\u2019t get them! They\u2019re for NPCs only. Ha-ha!\u201d Drives me nuts. I'm annoyed at the developers, not you.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554984#post1554984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Primal Utility <i>is</i> different from Prime, both in terms of some of the things it can't do (no manifesting swords made entirely out of Quintessence) and in terms of things it <i>can</i> do (until RBGtM, it held a monopoly on accessing Primal Ventures; and even now, it has the edge on making Wonders, as you only need three dots instead of four for Devices).</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">That\u2019s a very valid point, and as I\u2019m looking to create a quasi-Technomancer here I might try incorporating a Prime Sphere paradigm along those guidelines. That said, the character I have in mind would be more at home in Iteration X or the Void Engineers than at the Syndicate. More \u201cprivate inventor\u201d than \u201chypereconomist.\u201d Perhaps a bit of tweaking of Primal Utility to be less economically-focused. Maybe just call it Primal Energy and come up with something in between the usual Prime Sphere and the Primal Utility Sphere.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28819,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","user":"Arcanum Scholar","date":". 11-02-2025, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T20:24:17-08:00","id":1554997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554992#post1554992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, its role in magic item production is fairly critical, and at mastery level you're rolling in all the Quintessence you could ever ask for and can even nullify Paradox. As the foundational Sphere of magic, I've always prioritized it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the issue with Affinity Spheres though. Most people pick up Prime over time, because it a very useful Sphere (though it's not as useful for every character to have at high level compared to some of the others), but that's not the same as what the game incentivizes players to do; esp. if you want to make magical items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T23:31:29-08:00","id":1555000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554941#post1554941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I'm well aware they didn't include rules for this. That was my point - they <i><b>should</b></i> have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your anger, but there are other considerations to make when writing an RPG book.<br /> <br /> Outside any desire to make this NPC-exclusive (which is kinda lame, and <b>isn't</b> what they're doing), there are a few reasons to not make PC-oriented rules in the book:<br /> <br /> 1- Sometimes the concept is more important than making rules for how it happens to begin with. Making rules for how to establish a Technocratic Production Line that work as a universal guideline for every Mage game was certainly harder to do than it was worth;<br /> <br /> 2- There are things that must be a secret for setting reasons, like it or not. The ST is free to come up how Constructs are made, but almost no character knowing it was <i>the point</i>, or rather a part of it. Not even Union Agents know how those things work, this is setting design. In fact, to be clear, it's as true for NPCs as it is for PCs;<br /> <br /> 3- Defining how some things truly work impacts the kind of chronicle you're playing. We're talking something that directly impacts the main conflict of the setting, and that could have a million answers that each have a different effect on the game. Each answer opens the way to tell a different story, including the story of how the PCs will get their hands on this so important secret;<br /> <br /> 4- Another important consideration is at which point in the game will be a character able to get something if they have rules to do it. Is it really something a starting character should have been able to build themselves? Should they have it so soon with no strings attached? If not, when should they be able to make or procure such resource by themselves?<br /> <br /> You're also greatly ignoring that the game is built around the conflict between two organizations with their own advantages and disadvantages. The Technocracy is not &quot;the NPCs&quot;, and they don't have everything the Traditions have. They have a whole context in which they get access to those production lines, as they're not personal assets, they're special and tightly controlled. You <b>can</b> just make a Technocratic Agent, and in fact you can just have an abandoned production line you managed to make it work without having set it up yourself.<br /> <br /> No, I don't think they should have included those rules. They're unnecessary, and wouldn't easily make for the setting as they planned it. And you may want the setting differently or whatever, there are many ways to implement rules for this that help a particular chronicle, but that's beyond the scope of that book. I would personally prefer rules tailored to the particular game and story to be told rather than a standard for how to build an asset that should be virtually impossible to build.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554992#post1554992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, its role in magic item production is fairly critical, and at mastery level you're rolling in all the Quintessence you could ever ask for and can even nullify Paradox. As the foundational Sphere of magic, I've always prioritized it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And all that is completely irrelevant to Affinity Spheres, that's what Heavy Arms is trying to say.<br /> <br /> What an Affinity Sphere does is to slightly cut XP cost. Period. That's all. Your Prime 3 will be exactly the same be it Affinity or not.<br /> <br /> Since all you get out of it is a small XP cost reduction, and your starting points don't cost anything, your best return will come from having as Affinity a Sphere you start at 1.<br /> <br /> Even then, the difference is 3 XP at best. You'll save up 10 if you start at 1, 9 if you start at 2 and 7 if you start at three. Do with it what you will.<br /> <br /> Making your preferred Sphere an Affinity Sphere will only make it marginally faster to increase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T00:31:53-08:00","id":1555006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1555000#post1555000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- There are things that must be a secret for setting reasons, like it or not. The ST is free to come up how Constructs are made, but almost no character knowing it was <i>the point</i>, or rather a part of it. Not even Union Agents know how those things work, this is setting design. In fact, to be clear, it's as true for NPCs as it is for PCs;</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Technocracy is positively awash in Gadgets and Devices. If nobody knows how to make them, how did they get there? If the process of manufacturing them is so super-ultra-secret, there should be a lot less of them. More people making a wide variety of devices means more access to the manufacturing facilities. I've <i><b>worked</b></i> as a programmer in a manufacturing facility, and directly assisted both the people doing the designing and the people doing the manufacturing. It's not like they don't talk to each other - <i><b>constantly</b></i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1555000#post1555000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I don't think they should have included those rules. They're unnecessary, and wouldn't easily make for the setting as they planned it. And you may want the setting differently or whatever, there are many ways to implement rules for this that help a particular chronicle, but that's beyond the scope of that book. I would personally prefer rules tailored to the particular game and story to be told rather than a standard for how to build an asset that should be virtually impossible to build.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we'll have to agree to disagree. And I'll see about house-ruling something that makes sense for the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1555000#post1555000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bMaking your preferred Sphere an Affinity Sphere will only make it marginally faster to increase.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take what I can get. I also consider it <i><b>thematically</b></i> appropriate for an artificer to focus on Prime.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28819-arcanum-scholar","name":"Arcanum Scholar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T01:13:50-08:00","id":1555010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1555006#post1555006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Technocracy is positively awash in Gadgets and Devices. If nobody knows how to make them</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you completely missed the point where the difference isn't how you make Wonders, it's the facility itself.<br /> <br /> We're not talking about how the characters make their <i>Devices</i>. Technocracy characters use the same rules as everyone else. They can and do make their things in other places, and they follow the very same rules as everyone else when doing so, with the very same costs.<br /> <br /> The special Union facilities are what changes the costs and make mass production possible. And how to make <i>those</i> facilities is what Agents don't know.<br /> <br /> A Technomancer of any faction that comes across one such facility and can work with it will reap the same benefits, assuming the facility itself has everything it needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T02:21:48-08:00","id":1555015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1555006#post1555006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll take what I can get. I also consider it <i><b>thematically</b></i> appropriate for an artificer to focus on Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're kinda over-exaggerating Prime and under-playing how Ascension forces magic-item crafting into a multi-Sphere reliant activity. The setting is built to accommodate this by making it more of an NPC focus/PC goal rather than something PCs are expecting to be doing a lot of as a character focus. Starting or relatively low XP PCs are much better suited towards Trinkets (which might not even need Prime depending on what you're making) than being full on Wonder-smiths.<br /> <br /> There's also a reason why, in most editions, Matter is the &quot;artificer&quot; Sphere of choice. Thematically, the objects you make are the core of any sort of crafting character, and Matter is the Sphere of objects. Prime, without the context of Focus, can bind any effect into any object sure, but in the context of a Focus the object an effect is placed into matters to the mage. And Matter is the Sphere that makes creating the perfect vessels for your magical works easier. Matter lets you work Focus appropriate materials into otherwise impossible forms to combine form and magical-function. Much like when people think about throwing fireballs they think about Forces despite the default effect being Forces 3/Prime 2, Prime is ultimately the supporting Sphere here, not the one that maximizes your potential.<br /> <br /> You're not wrong to feel differently, but what you're expressing is also fighting the structure of the game instead of working with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-03T14:24:24-08:00","id":1555036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanum Scholar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1554935-artificer-build-for-mage?p=1554994#post1554994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Sorry, that\u2019s just a long-standing pet peeve of mine, going back decades at this point. I\u2019ve seen plenty of games where the developers go \u201cLook at these super cool things! And you don\u2019t get them! They\u2019re for NPCs only. Ha-ha!\u201d Drives me nuts. I'm annoyed at the developers, not you.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">That\u2019s a very valid point, and as I\u2019m looking to create a quasi-Technomancer here I might try incorporating a Prime Sphere paradigm along those guidelines. That said, the character I have in mind would be more at home in Iteration X or the Void Engineers than at the Syndicate. More \u201cprivate inventor\u201d than \u201chypereconomist.\u201d Perhaps a bit of tweaking of Primal Utility to be less economically-focused. Maybe just call it Primal Energy and come up with something in between the usual Prime Sphere and the Primal Utility Sphere.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Utility isn't an economic concept, per se. I could easily see an ItXer or VE wielding a Sphere that deals with examining the Utility of a thing, shaping that Utility, strengthening or weakening Utility, etc. Note that I said that having a Focus with Art of Desire or Hypereconomics is <i>usually</i> what's needed to access the variant Sphere of Primal Utility; but it doesn't <i>always </i>have to be that. Another approach would be to treat Utility as an emergent property of a complex system, an abstract measure of its ability to do useful things. Try to get away from the notion of thinking of it as a kind of energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}